<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5752" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bryon</span></b> , i, n.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρύον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Moss;</i> esp. the kind otherwise called sphagnos,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				12, 23, 50, § 108</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The grape - formed blossom of the silver
			poplar</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 28, 61, §
			132</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A plant growing upon the seashore</i>, <i>with leaves like lettuce</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 13,
				25, 49, § 137</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 8, 33, §
			56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 9, 36,
				§ 110</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
